{"qid":"Q1661685","names":["Sasanian Empire","Indo-Sasanian Empire"],"title":"Sasanian Empire","endonym":null,"capsule":"The Sasanian Empire was the last pre-Islamic Iranian empire, founded in 224 CE when Ardashir I defeated the Parthian king Artabanus IV at the Battle of Hormozdgan and established a new dynasty from the heartland of Fars. Ruling from Ctesiphon in Mesopotamia, the Sasanians made Zoroastrianism the state religion and for four centuries were Rome's and then Byzantium's principal rival across the Near East, contesting Armenia, the Caucasus, and the Mesopotamian frontier. The empire reached its greatest extent under Khosrow II (r. 590–628), briefly seizing the Levant, Egypt, and Anatolia before a ruinous defeat in the Byzantine–Sasanian War of 602–628 left it exhausted. Arab Muslim armies of the Rashidun Caliphate then shattered Sasanian power at al-Qadisiyyah (636) and Nahavand (642), and the last shah, Yazdegerd III, was killed in 651, ending Sasanian rule.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Territorial extent is reconstructed primarily from numismatic evidence (coin hoards and mint distributions) and limited textual sources; the boundaries shown are approximate and scholarly opinion varies on the extent of direct Kushano-Sasanian control versus Kidarite encroachment.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[],"britannica":null,"cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Sasanian Empire","rulers":[{"qid":null,"name":"Ardashir I","nativeName":"𐭠𐭥𐭲𐭧𐭱𐭲𐭥","roman":"Ardašīr I","start":224,"end":242,"image":null,"imageUrl":null,"imageLicense":null},{"qid":null,"name":"Shapur I","nativeName":"𐭱𐭧𐭯𐭥𐭧𐭥𐭩","roman":"Šābuhr I","start":